✅ SOLUTION OVERVIEW

We will:

1. ✅ Remove scroll from Radio


2. ✅ Control column width (TemplateSize)


3. ✅ Allow ONLY ONE scroll (outer container or gallery)




---

🧩 STEP 1: FIX RADIO SCROLL (MOST IMPORTANT)

Select Radio_Score

Set:

Width = Parent.TemplateWidth


---

Also set:

Wrap = true

👉 This prevents internal scrolling


---

OPTIONAL (if still scrolling):

Layout = Layout.Horizontal


---

🧩 STEP 2: CONTROL COLUMN WIDTH

Select Gallery_Questions_H AND Gallery_Header

Set BOTH:

TemplateSize = 110   // or 100–130 depending on design


---

🧩 STEP 3: REMOVE EXTRA SPACING

TemplatePadding = 0


---

🧩 STEP 4: CONTROL TOTAL WIDTH (IMPORTANT)

👉 You must decide:


---

OPTION A: ENABLE ONE SCROLL (Recommended 👍)

Let the header + rows scroll together

Set:

Gallery_Header.Width =
CountRows(Gallery_Header.AllItems) * Gallery_Header.TemplateSize

Same for:

Gallery_Questions_H.Width =
CountRows(Gallery_Questions_H.AllItems) * Gallery_Questions_H.TemplateSize

👉 This makes them expand → scroll appears ONLY once


---

OPTION B: FIT NO SCROLL (if few columns)

Gallery_Header.Width = Parent.Width - 270
Gallery_Questions_H.Width = Parent.Width - 270


---

🧩 STEP 5: CHECK CONTAINER OVERFLOW

Select HeaderContainer or parent container:

👉 Ensure it allows scroll (not clipping content)


---

🚨 MOST COMMON FIX (SUMMARY)

If you only do 3 things, do this:

// 1. Fix radio
Radio_Score.Width = Parent.TemplateWidth

// 2. Fix column width
Gallery_Questions_H.TemplateSize = 110
Gallery_Header.TemplateSize = 110

// 3. Expand gallery width
Gallery_Questions_H.Width =
CountRows(Gallery_Questions_H.AllItems) * 110


